From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:27:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 143/148] fix(refinery): the duplicate check searches open and
 in_progress bugs only (gcp-fooz4)

bd 1.3.0's search includes closed issues by default ("all statuses, including
closed") and accepts a comma-separated --status. Both facts invert the
premises behind gcp-h98d, which kept --status off the duplicate check because
search used to exclude closed and answer the comma form with []. On bd 1.3.x
the unfiltered check counts a fixed, closed bug as the duplicate, so a
regression of it is never filed and the refinery merges over it. The seat
measured it in a throwaway store (closed + in_progress + open "widget fails"
bugs): no filter -> 3, --status=open,in_progress -> 2, --status=open -> 1.

The formula's duplicate check now passes --status=open,in_progress, and its
comment says why. The drift guard is inverted: every gc bd search invocation
must name its statuses, a named list must include open and in_progress
(--status all stays writable), and the refinery's duplicate check must not
name closed or all. test_every_asset_bd_search_names_live_statuses and
test_refinery_duplicate_check_counts_only_live_bugs replace the two tests that
forbade the filter; both fail against the unfixed formula and pass after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
